!votekickViewer3D - changelog
=============================
Newest entries first. Versions start at 0.0.1.
Only new features and critical fixes are listed here; smaller changes and
tuning live in the git commit history. GitHub Releases get a distilled
version of this file (generated by scripts/release-notes.mjs).

0.0.2 - 2026-11-13
------------------
- Menu bar (File / View / Tools) in the floating pill style: Open,
  Grid/Wireframe with state checkmarks, Reset view, Settings, Plugins
  (stub for the planned custom user plugin system)
- File > Quit (hotkey Q) to close the app from the menu
- Editable hotkeys in Settings: click a binding, press the new
  combination (Esc cancels, Backspace clears). Defaults: Open = O,
  Wireframe = W, Grid = G, Reset view = R; physical keys, so Russian and
  English layouts work identically
- Localization: translations are plain <name>.json files in
  %APPDATA%\votekickViewer3D\lang - the english.json template is created
  on first launch, copy it, translate, rename; missing keys fall back to
  English
- "Launch maximized window" setting; default launch is a centered
  640x480 window that appears without a resize flash
- Error log: load failures append to log.txt next to the executable
  (AppData fallback when that is not writable); the uninstaller removes it
- Installer: choosing "Uninstall" for an already installed version now
  closes the installer after the uninstall completes
- View > Full screen (hotkey F) and View > Interface (hotkey H): the
  latter hides the whole UI, leaving only the 3D viewport for clean
  screenshots
- Mouse buttons can be bound as hotkeys (e.g. "Mouse Right", with
  modifiers like Ctrl+Mouse Left)
- About menu with the version and the project site (opens in the system
  browser)
- Opening a model closes any open dialog; Reset view fits the whole
  model on screen without changing the view angle
- Very large models: the file is read with a real progress bar, and
  parsing multi-hundred-MB files shows an explicit "this can take a
  while" status instead of looking frozen
- Large OBJ files (20 MB+) are parsed by a fast built-in parser straight
  from the file bytes: what took minutes with the generic loader now
  takes seconds (tested with a 626 MB / 3.4-million-vertex model)
- The status bar shows the triangle (polygon) count next to the file
  size, e.g. "model.obj  ·  5.1 MB  ·  12,345 polys"
- Menu items, dialog headers and the loading overlay got animated icons
  from the line-md set (MIT); they replay on every menu open
- View > Bounding box (hotkey B): wireframe cube edges around the whole
  model, recomputed when a new model loads
- The status bar shows the app version on the right plus icon indicators
  for the enabled View states (grid, wireframe, bounding box, full
  screen); the top-level menu buttons got icons too
- Blender-style numpad view controls: Num 1/3/7 (with Ctrl for the
  opposite side) snap to Front/Back/Left/Right/Top/Bottom and fit the
  model to the viewport the same way Reset view does, Num 5 toggles
  between perspective and orthographic projection with a matched on-screen
  scale, Num 2/4/6/8 orbit in 5 degree steps, Num +/- zooms and Num 9
  jumps to the opposite side; the directions are also in the View menu
- Settings > Always on top: keeps the window above all others, applies
  immediately and on the next launch
- FPS counter in the status bar (updated twice a second)
- Grid readability fix: grid and axis lines are no longer tone mapped,
  so they keep their exact colors next to any model; the center lines
  through the origin follow Blender's ground plane axes (X red, Z green)
  and the vertical axis uses the Blender color mapping (our up axis blue,
  our depth axis green)
- Settings > Colors: color pickers for the grid, wireframe and bounding
  box, applied live and persisted; the grid now draws as a solid overlay
  on top of the model instead of hiding behind it
- Wireframe mode renders all meshes with a single flat-colored material
  (color configurable in Settings) instead of per-material wireframes
- Reset view now also resets the orthographic zoom state, so the model
  is fitted to the window after wheel zooming in orthographic mode
- Fixed: the WebView2 default context menu (Back, Refresh, Save as,
  Print) no longer appears on right click, so the app page cannot be
  saved or reloaded from the UI
- Fixed: a startup crash in the grid color rebuild that prevented the
  menu bar and the model open handlers from ever being registered
- Wireframe is now an overlay: the solid textured model stays visible
  and the colored triangle edges are drawn on top of its surface
- Settings > Colors got a ShareX style color picker: saturation/value
  square, hue and alpha strips, RGB and alpha fields, hex field, a screen
  eyedropper (when the WebView supports it), recent colors (persisted)
  and a standard palette; the alpha part applies as line opacity
- The bounding box state is saved and restored across restarts like grid
  and wireframe
- The status bar shows the active projection (Perspective /
  Orthographic) next to the FPS counter
- Reset view fits the actual bounding box to the viewport with equal
  gaps on all four sides instead of its bounding sphere, so flat and
  elongated models no longer leave huge empty space around them; the fit
  solves the camera distance and the screen centering together
- Settings dialog redesigned with macOS style categories (General /
  Colors / Hotkeys) in a left sidebar and a close cross in the top left
- Custom tooltips for every control with a short delay (a third of a
  second), replacing the slow native title tooltips
- Help window (File > Help, hotkey F1): a dialog listing every hotkey,
  grouped into actions and numpad view controls, with a close cross in
  the top left that stays put while the list scrolls
- Menu items without an icon align with the icon column of the other
  items, so labels line up across the whole menu
- The color picker eyedropper button is removed; the picker keeps the
  square, strips, fields, recent colors and palette
- Tooltips open right above the cursor, centered on it; inside modal
  dialogs the bubble is shown above the dialog so it is never clipped
- The Settings dialog keeps a constant width when switching categories
- Fixed: Reset view right after a top/bottom numpad view left the camera
  rolled and off center (a stale camera up vector leaked into the fit)
- Fixed: leaving the orthographic projection after zooming in could clip
  the model; the matched scale now backs off to the full fit only when
  the matched view would not fit
- Fixed: reset view after orbiting or panning in the orthographic
  projection fitted along the stale direction (the inactive camera now
  always follows the active one, so the fit sees the rotated view)
- Fixed: perspective centering on close-up or flat models converged to a
  visible vertical offset (the per-corner depth weighting and the stop
  condition of the centering loop were corrected)
- The color picker eyedropper is an icon button now; it hides itself
  when the WebView rejects the screen capture, since the EyeDropper API
  reports support but fails on some WebView2 versions

0.0.1 - 2026-11-12
------------------
First public release.

- Model viewer for Windows: double-click .glb/.gltf/.fbx/.obj/.stl/.ply/.dae/
  .3ds in Explorer, or drag&drop into the window. Opening another model reuses
  the same window (single instance).
- Simple controls like a photo viewer: LMB orbit, RMB/MMB pan, wheel zoom,
  auto-framing on open; grid, wireframe, reset view (G / F / R / Ctrl+O).
  Settings (grid, wireframe, window size) persist in
  %APPDATA%\votekickViewer3D\cfg\settings.json.
- FBX/OBJ sidecar textures are picked up from the model's folder.
- NSIS installer (~1.7 MB) registers all 8 extensions and installs to the
  standard C:\Program Files\votekickViewer3D. Shortcuts (desktop, Start Menu),
  the Programs & Features entry and the publisher/author
  (!votekickAlex) carry the display name with the "!".
  The uninstaller's "delete app data" checkbox decides whether the settings
  and cache folder AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D (config + cache) is
  removed along with the program.
- Portable zip: votekickViewer3D-0.0.1-portable.zip, no installation needed.

0.0.1-dev - 2026-11-12 - detailed development history
-----------------------------------------------------
- Settings persistence (Milestone 3 start): settings.json lives in
  AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D\cfg, written safely by the backend
  (temp file + rename); frontend owns the schema in src/settings-schema.ts
  with named keys (view.grid, view.wireframe, window.width/height) and a
  deep-merge loader that ignores unknown keys - groundwork for the planned
  collapsible menu subitems and hotkeys
- Toolbar toggles (grid, wireframe) persist immediately (debounced 400 ms);
  the window size is saved on resize and restored by the backend on
  startup (LogicalSize, applied before first frame; implausible values
  ignored)
- Publisher fixed: bundle > publisher "!votekickAlex" (was auto-derived from
  the identifier as "votekick"); shown as the author in Programs & Features;
  the stale HKLM Software\votekick key from earlier builds is removed on
  uninstall
- Explorer is notified of association changes (SHChangeNotify /
  SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED via UPDATEFILEASSOC) in POSTINSTALL and POSTUNINSTALL
  hooks, so icons and "open with" entries refresh immediately instead of
  lingering in the Explorer icon cache after uninstall
- Uninstall hook removes the association "_backup" values the template
  restores-but-keeps under HKLM Software\Classes\.<ext>
- Installer overhaul (supersedes the earlier name/uninstall entries below):
  - Custom NSIS template (src-tauri/nsis/installer-template.nsi, based on the
    unmodified tauri-v2.12.4 installer.nsi, changes marked "; [votekick]"):
    shortcuts (desktop, Start Menu), installer title and the Programs &
    Features entry use DISPLAYNAME "!votekickViewer3D" with the "!", while
    PRODUCTNAME "votekickViewer3D" stays free of special characters for the
    install folder (C:\Program Files\votekickViewer3D) and registry keys
  - WebView2 profile moved out of the identifier folder
    (AppData\Local\com.votekick.viewer3d\EBWebView) into our tree via
    app > appDirectoriesOverride: localData $DATA/votekickViewer3D/cache/webview
    -> AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D\cache\webview\EBWebView
  - Uninstall hook (src-tauri/installer-hooks.nsh) honors the uninstaller's
    "delete app data" checkbox again: checked = remove
    AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D (settings + cache), unchecked = keep;
    the legacy identifier folder is always removed as non-user data
- Uninstaller always removes AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D via the
  POSTUNINSTALL hook (src-tauri/installer-hooks.nsh); the template's built-in
  "delete app data" checkbox stays visible but has no effect on our layout
- Display name "!votekickViewer3D" (productName) drives the window title,
  Start Menu / desktop shortcuts and the C:\Program Files\!votekickViewer3D
  install folder; mainBinaryName "votekickViewer3D" keeps artifact file names
  free of special characters; installer/uninstaller embed the app icon
- Data layout decision: cfg always in AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D\cfg
  (never next to the exe); cache in ...\cache; log file next to the exe
  with automatic fallback to AppData\Roaming\votekickViewer3D when Program
  Files is not writable; the app creates the cfg/cache folders on first
  launch; uninstalling always removes the AppData data folder
- Installer milestone: NSIS bundle with file associations for
  .glb/.gltf/.fbx/.obj/.stl/.ply/.dae/.3ds, per-machine install (default
  C:\Program Files\!votekickViewer3D), portable zip build, artifacts collected
  into release/ by scripts/collect-release.mjs (`npm run release`)
- collect-release.mjs fails on duplicate installer artifacts so stale bundle
  files can never overwrite fresh ones in release/
- scripts/collect-release.mjs + `npm run release` build the installer and
  portable zip into release/ (kept out of git; binaries ship via Releases)
- Fixed: command line arguments are only accepted when they end with a
  supported model extension (dev tooling flags no longer trip the loader)

0.0.1-dev - 2026-11-12
----------------------
- Milestone 2 (commit 1d96976): opening models from the OS
  - file path from command line args reaches the frontend with no startup race
  - single instance: a second launch routes the file to the running window,
    focuses it and replaces the shown model (no second window, ever)
  - models load from any folder via the Tauri asset protocol
  - FBX/OBJ sidecar textures resolve relative to the model's folder
  - window title shows the loaded file name; load errors land in the status bar
- Milestone 1 (commit 48483ab): viewer core
  - Tauri 2 shell, vanilla-ts frontend, Three.js renderer
  - OrbitControls: LMB orbit, RMB/MMB pan, wheel zoom; damping enabled
  - auto-framing via bounding sphere (vertical + horizontal FOV aware)
  - drag&drop + file dialog loading: GLB, GLTF, FBX, OBJ, STL, PLY, DAE, 3DS
  - toolbar: Open, Grid, Wireframe, Reset view; keys G / F / R / Ctrl+O
  - loading overlay with progress, status line
  - app icon generated from logo.png; display name "!votekickViewer3D"
